# Gate 2's ratchet floor. See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-phase2-go-relay-design.md
# (Stage 2a > Gate 2) and docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-10-phase2-2a7-coverage-gate.md.
#
# `missing` is the ratchet -- a MAXIMUM, not a target, and lower is better. It is set
# from the WORST run of at least twelve on the tree that earned it, which is why this
# gate carries no separate tolerance parameter: the measured spread is already inside
# the number. Four regions are known to flap (owner-side coordinated stop, non-owner
# local cleanup, the stderr-reader join, _wait_for_channel_ready's error branch) and
# the list has grown twice; a fixed tolerance would be stale on arrival.
#
# `shape` and `statements` are EQUALITY checks, not comparisons. A different measurement
# shape or module list makes two numbers incomparable rather than better or worse, and
# the gate says so instead of ratcheting.
#
# Written by:  scripts/coverage_live_path.sh --write-floor
# Enforced by: scripts/coverage_live_path.sh --gate  (backend-tests.yml, job coverage-gate)
#
# PROVENANCE (Phase 2 PR 2a-7, Task 7). `missing` below is the WORST of 21 rounds
# under the per-container/v1-sysmon shape, NOT the figure --write-floor's own run
# happened to produce (2009) and NOT a median -- hand-set after the write, per the
# plan's Task 7 Step 4. Tree: 41f8021a12e3210d50ee4871cbdfecc1647aa89c (2a-7's branch,
# all four coverage PRs plus Tasks 1-7 committed). Measured 2026-09-10 against
# dispatcharr-testrunner-2a7-{proxy,liveproxy,channels}, three containers, one label
# each. Stopping rule (maximum unchanged for >=6 consecutive rounds, minimum 12) was
# met at round 12 and held through round 20; rounds continued to 20 for margin, per
# the same over-run judgement Task 1 used. Full sequence, in order:
#   2041 2005 2026 2039 2024 2035 2008 2044 2013 2032 2028
#   2026 2003 2026 2033 2025 2028 2028 2029 2023 2023
# max=2044 (round 7)  min=2003 (round 12)  spread=41  n=21
# The tree's denominator (7978) is unchanged from Task 1's merged-tree measurement,
# but this is a DIFFERENT measurement, not a re-run of it: Task 1's floor candidate
# was 2048 on the tree before Tasks 3/4 added two tests (row 29's and row 30's), and
# this one is 2044 -- 4 statements lower, on a tree with slightly more covered, not a
# discrepancy between two measurements of the same thing.
#
# HOW TO MOVE THIS FLOOR (read before running --write-floor). `--write-floor` writes
# the figure from the run it JUST took -- one run, not the worst of N -- because the
# floor policy (worst of >=12 rounds under a stopping rule; see the top of this file)
# lives in the stopping-rule PROCEDURE, not in the script. The two are not the same
# thing by design, and `--write-floor` cannot know it is being run for the Nth time in
# a campaign versus once, so it never guesses at "worst so far" on your behalf. The
# exact sequence, every time this floor legitimately moves:
#   1. Run scripts/coverage_live_path_isolated.sh --report repeatedly (a fresh
#      container per round -- see Task 1/7 of the coverage-gate plan) until the
#      MAXIMUM `missing` has been unchanged for >=6 consecutive rounds, >=12 total.
#      Record every round, in order -- a bare min/max cannot show the rule was met.
#   2. Take max(runs). That number, not any single run's own figure, is what belongs
#      in `missing` below.
#   3. Run --write-floor once (writable checkout or a scratch rw container -- /repo is
#      read-only in the standard test-hook container) to get the correct FILE FORMAT,
#      shape and statements fields machine-produced.
#   4. Hand-edit `missing` to max(runs) from step 2 if it differs from what
#      --write-floor's own run produced (it usually will -- one run is rarely the
#      worst of N), and recompute `percent` = (1 - missing/statements) * 100 to match.
#      This hand-edit is the honest, documented step, not a workaround: teaching
#      --write-floor to accept an explicit override was considered for this PR and
#      declined, because the value would have to thread through both the regression
#      check (which run's `missing` counts as "worse than the floor"?) and the percent
#      computation (recomputed for which value?), which is more machinery-in-the-gate
#      than this PR wants to risk for a maintainer action taken rarely and by hand.
#   5. Re-run --gate from the ordinary READ-ONLY test-hook container -- the shape CI
#      actually runs it in -- and confirm it exits 0 against the new floor before
#      committing.
shape=per-container/v1-sysmon
statements=7978
missing=2044
percent=74.38
measured=2026-09-10
runs=21
